  "question": {
    "text": "On the ellipse <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>8</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math>,&nbsp;let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></math> be a point in the second quadrant such that the tangent at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></math> to the ellipse is perpendicular to the line <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>. Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></msup></math> be the foci of the ellipse and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>e</mi></math> be its eccentricity. If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> is the area of the triangle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>SPS</mi><mo>'</mo></msup></math>,&nbsp;then&nbsp;the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>-</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#183;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> is"
  },
  "options": [
    {
